<h1>Outreach Center</h1>

<p>
    The Outreach Center is where you plan, create, and manage email campaigns. Whether you're sending newsletters, renewal reminders, or marketing messages, the Outreach Center helps you reach the right people with the right message at the right time.
</p>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Full-page screenshot of the Outreach Center showing campaign cards with status indicators (Scheduled, Running, Finished) and metrics. Show the campaign list/grid layout with counts and status badges. Include labels for key areas. -->

<h2>Understanding Campaigns</h2>

<p>
    A campaign is a planned email send to a group of recipients. Each campaign has:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>A template</strong> – The email content (subject, body, images)</li>
    <li><strong>A segment</strong> – Who will receive the email (filtered list of clients/leads)</li>
    <li><strong>A schedule</strong> – When it will be sent</li>
    <li><strong>A status</strong> – Where it is in the process (Draft, Scheduled, Running, Finished)</li>
</ul>

<p>
    Campaigns help you send consistent, professional emails to many people at once while tracking who received what and when.
</p>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Visual diagram showing the components of a campaign: Template + Segment + Schedule = Campaign. Use boxes and arrows to show how these pieces fit together. Include icons or simple illustrations for each component. -->

<h2>Campaign Status and Health</h2>

<p>
    Each campaign card shows its status and key metrics at a glance:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Scheduled</strong> – Campaign is set up and waiting to start</li>
    <li><strong>Running</strong> – Campaign is actively sending emails</li>
    <li><strong>Finished</strong> – Campaign has completed sending</li>
    <li><strong>Draft</strong> – Campaign is being created but not ready to send</li>
</ul>

<p>
    You'll also see quick metrics like:
</p>

<ul>
    <li>How many emails were sent</li>
    <li>How many were delivered</li>
    <li>How many bounced or failed</li>
    <li>Recent send activity</li>
</ul>

<p>
    This helps you spot issues quickly and understand campaign performance at a glance.
</p>

