<h2>Blasters</h2>

<p>
    A "blaster" is the system that actually sends your emails. Think of it as the email delivery engine. Quickfire uses email delivery providers (like Microsoft Graph) to send campaigns.
</p>

<p>
    <strong>Key concepts:</strong>
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Delivery provider</strong> – The service that sends the emails (configured per campaign)</li>
    <li><strong>Throttling</strong> – The system limits how fast emails are sent to avoid being flagged as spam</li>
    <li><strong>Batch processing</strong> – Emails are sent in batches rather than all at once</li>
    <li><strong>Rate limits</strong> – Daily, hourly, and total send limits to protect your sending reputation</li>
</ul>

<p>
    The blaster handles all the technical details of sending emails reliably and safely.
</p>

