<h2>Segments</h2>

<p>
    Segments define who receives your campaign. They're filtered lists of clients or leads based on criteria you specify.
</p>

<p>
    <strong>Segment criteria examples:</strong>
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>By product type</strong> – All clients with Workers' Comp policies</li>
    <li><strong>By expiration date</strong> – Policies expiring in the next 30 days</li>
    <li><strong>By location</strong> – Clients in a specific state or city</li>
    <li><strong>By status</strong> – Active clients, new leads, etc.</li>
    <li><strong>By custom fields</strong> – Any other criteria you've set up</li>
</ul>

<p>
    Segments are saved in the Library so you can reuse them. For example, you might have a "Renewals This Month" segment that you use for multiple campaigns.
</p>

